Chapter: PatternProgressGuard
  cites Foreword chapter Maybe
  cites Foreword chapter Pattern

 Track D item 19, the Pattern leg. Two defects, both measured before a line was
 written.

 pat-match-many recursed on whatever position its inner pattern left it at,
 without requiring that the position MOVE. A pattern that matches zero
 characters therefore repeats forever, accumulating acc & r.mr-value on a heap
 with no collector: many (lit "") reaches OUT OF MEMORY in about seven seconds.

 It is reachable from text. pattern "many optional" is two ordinary English
 words: "many" takes pat-parse-many-of, "optional" at the end of the token list
 falls to pat-parse-optional's i >= n case which answers PatLiteral "", and the
 result is PatMany (PatLiteral ""). Those two words exhaust the heap.

 pat-match-repeat answered mr-consumed = pos, the ABSOLUTE position, where every
 other matcher answers a relative count. At position 0 the two coincide, which
 is why the existing test never saw it. At any other position the caller
 advances by position-plus-count and overshoots: and-then (lit "ab") of
 and-then (exactly 2 digit) (lit "cd") did NOT match "ab12cd".

 Row 4 is the discriminator for the count fix: the position-0 case was already
 correct and must not move. Rows 1 to 3 and 7 are the ordinary controls.

Section: Body

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni ("1-digits " & show (pat-test digits "123"))
    print-line-uni ("2-extract " & pat-extract (many1 letter) "abc123")
    print-line-uni ("3-find " & show (pat-find digits "abc123"))
    print-line-uni ("4-repeat-at-0 " & format-match (pat-match (exactly 3 digit) "12345" 0))
    print-line-uni ("5-repeat-at-2 " & format-match (pat-match (exactly 2 digit) "ab12cd" 2))
    print-line-uni ("6-seq-nested " & format-match (pat-match (and-then (lit "ab") (and-then (exactly 2 digit) (lit "cd"))) "ab12cd" 0))
    print-line-uni ("7-parse-letters " & show (pat-test (pattern "letters") "abc"))
    print-line-uni ("8-many-empty " & format-match (pat-match (many (lit "")) "abc" 0))
    print-line-uni ("9-parse-many-optional " & show (pat-test (pattern "many optional") "abc"))
  end

